---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
const repo = 'https://github.com/charifmahmoudi/mobile-ot-security-assessment';
---
<SiteLayout title="Customer Pilot — Atlas OT Scout" description="A bounded Atlas evaluation starts with one real OT evidence question, a defined process area, authorized evidence methods and measurable customer value.">
  <section class="bg-ink text-white"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-20 sm:px-8 lg:py-28"><p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-atlas">Customer pilot</p><h1 class="mt-5 max-w-4xl text-5xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.05em] sm:text-6xl">Start with one real OT evidence question.</h1><p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-white/60">For example: <span class="text-white">Does the installed control equipment in Pumping Area A match the inventory currently accepted by operations?</span></p></div></section>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-20 sm:px-8"><div class="grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2"><div class="rounded-3xl border border-ink/10 bg-surface p-7 sm:p-8"><p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-steel">Customer provides</p><ul class="mt-7 space-y-4 text-lg"><li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-atlas">01</span><span>One defined site and process area</span></li><li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-atlas">02</span><span>The existing accepted asset baseline</span></li><li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-atlas">03</span><span>Operational context and responsible stakeholders</span></li><li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-atlas">04</span><span>Approved evidence sources or capture access</span></li><li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-atlas">05</span><span>Authorization, exclusions and stop conditions</span></li></ul></div><div class="rounded-3xl bg-graphite p-7 text-white sm:p-8"><p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-atlas">P0-WATER assessment unit</p><div class="mt-7 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm"><div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/[.045] p-4"><strong class="block text-2xl">1</strong><span class="mt-2 block text-white/45">site / process area</span></div><div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/[.045] p-4"><strong class="block text-2xl">1</strong><span class="mt-2 block text-white/45">L2 segment / VLAN</span></div><div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/[.045] p-4"><strong class="block text-2xl">≤64</strong><span class="mt-2 block text-white/45">imported asset records</span></div><div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/[.045] p-4"><strong class="block text-2xl">≤256</strong><span class="mt-2 block text-white/45">observed endpoints</span></div><div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/[.045] p-4"><strong class="block text-2xl">≤16</strong><span class="mt-2 block text-white/45">allowlisted active targets</span></div><div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/[.045] p-4"><strong class="block text-2xl">≤4h</strong><span class="mt-2 block text-white/45">field collection</span></div></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="bg-surface"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-20 sm:px-8"><p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-steel">Assessment</p><h2 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] sm:text-5xl">A controlled workflow, not an open-ended technology trial.</h2><ol class="mt-12 grid gap-3 md:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-6">{[['01','Prepare'],['02','Collect'],['03','Review'],['04','Reconcile'],['05','Assess'],['06','Finalize']].map(([n,label]) => <li class="rounded-2xl border border-ink/10 bg-paper p-5"><span class="font-mono text-xs text-atlas">{n}</span><strong class="mt-8 block">{label}</strong></li>)}</ol><p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-steel">The least intrusive adequate evidence source is used for the documented question. Active identity work is limited to explicitly approved targets and operations.</p></div></section>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-20 sm:px-8"><div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2"><div><p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-steel">Customer receives</p><h2 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em]">An answer that can be reviewed and acted on.</h2></div><ul class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">{['Reconciled asset baseline','Exceptions and unresolved questions','Evidence-linked findings','Visibility and assessment limitations','Active-operation ledger where applicable','Reviewed assessment package'].map((x) => <li class="rounded-2xl border border-ink/10 bg-surface p-5 font-semibold">{x}</li>)}</ul></div></section>
  <section class="bg-ink text-white"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 py-20 sm:px-8"><p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-atlas">Success criterion</p><h2 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] sm:text-5xl">Did Atlas produce a materially more trustworthy view of the bounded OT area than the customer started with?</h2><p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-white/55">A pilot is useful when discrepancies become clearer, evidence behind conclusions is inspectable, limitations are explicit, and the result improves a real operational or professional decision.</p><div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="rounded-full bg-atlas px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-ink" href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/business-development/OFFER.md`}>Review evaluation terms</a><a class="rounded-full border border-white/15 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold" href={`${repo}/wiki`}>Open the Wiki</a></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
